In Progress (v1.0 core shipped) — re-promoted from Deferred

SafeMod was previously deferred over GDPR Article 9 (special-category
mental-health data) liability for a solo maintainer. The shipped crate
designs that liability out:

- zero dependencies; #![forbid(unsafe_code)]
- stores no identifiers, reads no clock, performs no I/O — it cannot
  persist or transmit anything
- wellbeing reporting is aggregate-only with a k-anonymity minimum cohort
  (>=5); worst-case data-at-rest is an integer count, which is not
  special-category data

Surface (all three README promises implemented + tested, 17 tests green):
- render:   blur/grayscale/mute-by-default, time-boxed reveals
- limits:   per-shift item cap, continuous-exposure cap, mandatory breaks
- wellbeing: anonymous ordinal signals -> aggregate, cohort-gated report
- Session:  ties reveal policy + exposure tracker into one gate

CI: in the Rust workspace; cargo fmt --check, clippy -D warnings, and
cargo test all pass.

Next (v1.x): an integration example wiring SafeMod into a concrete review
queue (e.g. Bluesky Ozone); optional WASM build for browser review tools.
